wer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c7df08-a8c0-585f-9280-89506d78dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461194} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2276e8-6e00-56fc-98dd-dbbff77f2df5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08a8dbc9-b97f-57b3-acad-4c86f2f3f516" :question/math-academy-id "q-101983" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc27a54ac20efc84bfbc404a20a91309c60c3fb42118f164129e93eee584437b.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function is continuous at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=-5$\n- The function is differentiable at $x=0$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement III  is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512f4d7d-a50e-5ac1-9b00-a23a2f1e85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461195} {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3434df-a85b-5891-9fca-5190f4d5b98e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd91feb-5abf-5ad2-b1f4-c8b98678090d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} :answer-field/id #uuid "09fa150b-0bcd-5369-b4b9-9a606723ef7f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd1d8db-a0f8-5a3f-9666-d01d5c0ea372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9afc227-2585-54bd-9518-4d409658168b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efd9ac2b-7a32-57f6-9899-3da1aeffaa13" :question/math-academy-id "q-102666" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n\nII. $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n\nIII. $C={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3743095-b86d-5690-811f-9531139d1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461201} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac7323d-37e2-59e4-a0ab-792785d6d9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3743095-b86d-5690-811f-9531139d1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461201} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e0d85d4-3c22-5afa-997d-194a34f411f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1380862d-ca0a-5272-9181-d311561d8806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461203} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3e85aa-6154-5b67-b61a-417273e8e291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3e85aa-6154-5b67-b61a-417273e8e291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461204} :answer-field/id #uuid "4887cf56-6456-5833-b629-a8cf9dec498f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462355} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8048f25f-64aa-5f39-88e5-04a81280042c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461205} {:answer/id #uuid "49ca8a54-1d01-5b3f-b737-4ae82e38a518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8048f25f-64aa-5f39-88e5-04a81280042c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461205} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f5cd5df-6278-5c4d-b889-1bdbfb2580bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c35a4d59-f293-5742-bd9e-003fa5d50c23" :question/math-academy-id "q-102669" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eccb9532-7de2-59e7-a82e-6ab5c5c256d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461207} {:answer/id #uuid "a25d5fdd-a31e-51b5-a9cb-b9b85d9e48e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a25d5fdd-a31e-51b5-a9cb-b9b85d9e48e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461208} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04379d-5378-57ac-8c8a-5c79d6defc9c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a26ee96-ebd3-5ef0-a937-f4248c9f7f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461209} {:answer/id #uuid "7a779c6b-ec23-5c8c-8565-47792308afae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a26ee96-ebd3-5ef0-a937-f4248c9f7f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a3a0ee6-e7ec-58ca-a7bd-fe2195a3acfc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeb9f5d1-a68b-53b2-8b45-266c26e51dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461211} {:answer/id #uuid "c61e9668-9427-5911-9597-cfb248789995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c61e9668-9427-5911-9597-cfb248789995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461212} :answer-field/id #uuid "9af69d4d-34e6-541a-a6e6-dbacb78cccfe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67a1c719-c84d-5d17-9d41-c30fb7529952" :question/math-academy-id "q-102670" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf47f24-5826-503b-9314-2ce4fcb361ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461213} {:answer/id #uuid "66e828c3-1224-5037-bfe0-efa2537a90f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf47f24-5826-503b-9314-2ce4fcb361ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461213} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b58693c-bbc8-5575-a394-e3f95bcc8188" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511ed65d-c16a-5cf1-8eff-ed8add12d24d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461215} {:answer/id #uuid "906f776b-127c-521a-9b6b-7181b210e977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461216}] :answer-fie