3f9-5815-a23d-64900cd2d836" :question/math-academy-id "q-102675" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e961e28-39a7-5737-ac2b-099fbae2e86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/id