:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461235} :answer-field/id #uuid "c92498fe-844f-5d91-b3e3-084780e00322" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "343b3c1e-da90-580a-91f6-9c9756fee1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-103150" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-5$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-2$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-5,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-5,-1].$\n\n![](images/7d/7d68a4bd81717c3ad663fc85c45dfce62217a046f683cc92a6869f87ff3b166a.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $-2\\in (-5,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $1\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce59552-42d8-50fa-a897-42349ebc16b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461237} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb50c65-9777-5d34-aa33-37b64205dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce59552-42d8-50fa-a897-42349ebc16b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461237} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb608e3-5b5a-5e3b-999f-d2563700f5de" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48763910-2d7e-5c19-a141-501b2718c16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461239} {:answer/id #uuid "be4475de-8ca5-5c08-ac5b-ef0839ad6e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48763910-2d7e-5c19-a141-501b2718c16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461239} :answer-field/id #uuid "04846c1b-e0e5-55ca-b43d-b9dac2441726" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d5145db-c8f3-5a11-bcac-ba051dfd7c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461241} {:answer/id #uuid "12406a8e-a857-514f-8e52-e7ec0c770dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d5145db-c8f3-5a11-bcac-ba051dfd7c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461241} :answer-field/id #uuid "f30ac93d-bc21-5c63-abea-26c7dd4ea0fd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "21ccde81-8669-5255-b2ed-8bdddd923bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-103152" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-5)^{n}$ converges at  $x=2,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series diverges at $x=6$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=0$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=8$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=5,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[2,8).$\n\n![](images/df/dfd59d22892764c4da387d48b07a6a1069ea59e13be75cd099d21ce53975d64c.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $6\\in [2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=6.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $0\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $8\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the listed.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "753c6bc4-8bc9-5bc4-9b17-0e7b5a4fa7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461243} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9cf866-8180-5637-bc9a-8cedd8a64adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9cf866-8180-5637-bc9a-8cedd8a64adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461244} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e3870e-c98a-5c4e-b773-7c15a2ad964f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f022f9a-3577-5071-863a-b61b2a5743ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461245} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c4a3d-ac96-5582-8173-7504b99c0b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd2c4a3d-ac96-5582-8173-7504b99c0b74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461246} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a988df-c939-58e6-bed2-1175955dc667" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "895d153f-7cd2-5072-b3ca-0e8cae1d45a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461247} {:answer/id #uuid "7de099d9-85b8-5974-a14f-c84279cd5b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "895d153f-7cd2-5072-b3ca-0e8cae1d45a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461247} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbcaf317-42fe-583d-9d07-58b3779f0c9b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "93c0e2ef-7f5e-5e9b-aac8-f784a726661a" :question/math-academy-id "q-103169" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=2$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=1$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{5}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{5}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,4).$\n\n![](images/d0/d01788625c7b429a15caf441c6a651fa92281dc544f99c544bdb12f9d8b6f032.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $2\\in [-1,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=2.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $1\\in [-1,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement III is not necessarily true. The given information guarantees convergence for points strictly between $-1$ and $4$, but it does not guarantee convergence at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} {:answer/id #uuid "529614bd-8f87-5f2c-80b4-5c37e138c066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c392bd2e-f2f9-5ceb-b0b1-f3a1b122ab52" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c50d44-335d-5651-ba10-b49f0f37fe9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461251} {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce112048-db7b-58d9-ac72-bb8feec404bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} {:answer/id #uuid "ace51aeb-e1da-564d-aaa1-10285b642108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} :answer-field/id #uuid "72accc2e-3370-511e-9b00-a598c293557b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76850d0b-0e5d-5926-80f5-97253aff4b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103170" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+7)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-3,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n- **I.** The series converges at $x=-11$\n- **II.** The series converges at $x=-8$\n- **III.** The series converges at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-7,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-3,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $4,$ i.e., $R\\ge 4.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-11,-3].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-11,-3].$\n\n![](images/47/4764256e5f00e7a11d688bd99d5fa1c22db819e7a188113f0ef4cd987a9b7595.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-11\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $-8\\in (-11,-3],$ the series is convergent at $x=-8.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $1\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090fc51b-4d12-5f60-88f8-ac5a4b13097b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461255} {:answer/id #uuid "4a490cbe-a1fc-5779-866a-04511c2d89df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a490cbe-a1fc-5779-866a-04511c2d89df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461256} :answer-field/id #uuid "4660fa26-6eb4-552c-b659-a5bb3fdb38e2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203315ab-b883-5cf3-9e0f-dc0d51fd720c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461257} {:answer/id #uuid "2140d6dd-0dab-5e0c-9b15-f877af212e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2140d6dd-0dab-5e0c-9b15-f877af212e2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00a579e-e820-57de-ab22-60410abdcf00" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba813b06-d5fe-5f56-8fdc-f1ae37721250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461259} {:answer/id #uuid "19534c2b-71f9-5560-90e2-02c8041640df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19534c2b-71f9-5560-90e2-02c8041640df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461260} :answer-field/id #uuid "19628958-a21d-5f53-ae89-d685f932baef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59bba89f-5fae-5f25-a8be-5a25060edfd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-103172" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n- **I.** $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$\n- **II.** $3{y}^{2}$\n- **III.** $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y).$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2})=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1))=0=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)$ gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f503f6-69a7-5d68-a11b-13f00bdd16f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461261} {:answer/id #uuid "848dd2d6-6e77-557c-b98a-f43e6b7db9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6f503f6-69a7-5d68-a11b-13f00bdd16f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461261} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc41026f-42e8-5b54-9417-9d6b477e89f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f1fd05-76fc-5b99-a0c2-a90083805755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461263} {:answer/id #uuid "0f1f0dd1-4635-59a8-8716-ef1056569f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f1f0dd1-4635-59a8-8716-ef1056569f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461264} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b91d6b1-05d5-5e41-9dba-2acad420c227" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "106f08f9-0740-5a25-acd7-bad0545e6965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461265} {:answer/id #uuid "427fad5f-6fec-57c1-9ac0-73467afa5d48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "106f08f9-0740-5a25-acd7-bad0545e6965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461265} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1e2b2a-3495-573d-8c25-cae8e1c5c279" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d411ceca-268e-5683-adfb-764387aebbdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103174" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\n2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $Q(x,y)?$\n- **I.** $6x{y}^{2}$\n- **II.** $3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$\n- **III.** $2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $P(x,y)=2x{y}^{3}.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{3})=6x{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂x}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6x{y}^{2})=6{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=6x{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2})=6x{y}^{2}=\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{3}{y}^{2})=6{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\ne \\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''II only''."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147499 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Factors Giving an Exact ODE"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6cba8d6-c415-53ab-badb-6bf8dbbbd0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461267} {:answer/id #uuid "319d8d6d-e36c-5d92-9294-5c3e0ebc3a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319d8d6d-e36c-5d92-9294-5c3e0ebc3a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461268} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d85e36-2f10-523d-8a99-52889142a7c1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b07408-8bfc-50ff-a374-c9d5ffa3c8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461269} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7fd223-bf94-5026-8a1f-ea7d0c2bf194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7b07408-8bfc-50ff-a374-c9d5ffa3c8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461269} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5efdf9e-1d50-589f-8cc5-55517cb057ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40734f81-131a-5471-b8b3-e03ea290a58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461271} {:answer/id #uuid "2a6b4205-de62-57e6-aad8-a56544ae9904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40734f81-131a-5471-b8b3-e03ea290a58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461271} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b089f27-1db2-55de-a28d-d2d13e8068fe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ffb478e-6d0e-5395-bbb6-0e1bbace63ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-103175" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n- **I.** ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$\n- **II.** $-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\n- **III.** ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ gives an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2})=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-2y\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-{y}^{2}$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''I only''."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ca57ad-6a39-5da3-a0a2-57aecb6d47fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461273} {:answer/id #uuid "8774e632-f450-599c-8ad5-4217f5858897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8774e632-f450-599c-8ad5-4217f5858897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461274} :answer-field/id #uuid "af89ebc7-578c-59cc-8ba0-af951c2a1619" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462390} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822e6b63-fdce-5fbe-b767-c309319945b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461275} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f48b58-20d7-5c59-a34c-5a2382d9ccf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f48b58-20d7-5c59-a34c-5a2382d9ccf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461276} :answer-field/id #uuid "a36aef3b-008a-5af0-a829-ec2cab51c8aa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462391} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa66ed42-00b7-5149-afa9-e61ddf9c0006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461277} {:answer/id #uuid "549d9b59-93c0-5e2d-aa3a-dc11d548a49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa66ed42-00b7-5149-afa9-e61ddf9c0006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461277} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbae254d-0fe9-5642-9e45-73b127b734b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f635edc1-2f85-538f-89d8-4edf62a22ccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-103437" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb61c048eb7eac87f82c53717f8f67251b59610817ddf1f267e80543c0c86959.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=-1$\n\nII. $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\n\nIII. $f(x)$ has a local maximum at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=-1,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(-1)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a critical point at $x=-1$ since each stationary point is a critical point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a local minimum at $x=-1$ since $f(-1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b293e62f-6f87-5e32-9d47-30001e75a473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461279} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8359a-378f-5d30-b9c0-f8c4d4fb9c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8359a-378f-5d30-b9c0-f8c4d4fb9c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461280} :answer-field/id #uuid "92f57ac4-00e1-5c7e-9979-b50b20bf610f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462393} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6cc80e1-8c2d-50ca-9f1e-11ffa91bfdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461281} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3f2ac5-9e21-5c73-81bb-3e709f16ae1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3f2ac5-9e21-5c73-81bb-3e709f16ae1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461282} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c3c88f-d59c-59fa-bfdc-8de1c22722c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a4c59c3-0fa7-57fd-a77c-691d443f258c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461283} {:answer/id #uuid "9d12003a-0d3f-510e-b2aa-cfbebcab6a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d12003a-0d3f-510e-b2aa-cfbebcab6a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461284} :answer-field/id #uuid "37ed8c1c-74af-5b75-8c3b-0d241ae04ccb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2c02942-de68-547a-8bfa-7932a2f390a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103438" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5bbb0cacbe8dca2facfd49e757ba9b7aa40ee91ae820f001c72d637186d57b79.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- $f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$\n- $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement II is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1$ since $f(1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} {:answer/id #uuid "6f47c9f4-cfdf-51cc-a8ee-2e312b6e2ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42517c5-86d0-573b-9c42-a43146a898c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} {:answer/id #uuid "19f14dea-5bfb-587c-9cb9-670c75f65f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac105e7-89d8-52b0-b5e6-9803aa72f310" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} {:answer/id #uuid "5df81d82-6062-53b0-8ac4-34d404968f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} :answer-field/id #uuid "4deab2df-6f34-5f4c-8d22-c93a07225cea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d00cc33e-d21d-57ae-828a-16fa83891b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-104357" :question/problem "![](images/30/30df82b4c47905fd8277067f9207a5e970a96d8ec386879d2872b5f5c3d8dd3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7746b1d-22e8-5721-a847-a60ad72b51b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461291} {:answer/id #uuid "6f612c3f-7d07-5916-b27a-0ee2c0892bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f612c3f-7d07-5916-b27a-0ee2c0892bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461292} :answer-field/id #uuid "185d1bc6-a657-522f-ac8d-c850091c6096" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea896e26-9386-5908-ac83-14e845a51e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461293} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bc51d4-60a3-56e9-8ffa-561c2473ec84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea896e26-9386-5908-ac83-14e845a51e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461293} :answer-field/id #uuid "104ab594-bb0f-570d-ba4f-199833a1413a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462400} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8c9af3a-b58a-58ce-9031-b2ea444bdc21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461295} {:answer/id #uuid "655f48f9-ffa9-55ff-81a1-eda4162a6758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8c9af3a-b58a-58ce-9031-b2ea444bdc21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461295} :answer-field/id #uuid "9710139d-ff9c-5dce-a5ea-04016adbbf09" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fc756662-eff5-518b-9ac2-39ac467a0419" :question/math-academy-id "q-104358" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c95fb061d6b860655e934f2691d03e53f7bb77a617200f523f1695ee49083fe.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=1,$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)=4=f(1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false.  The function is not right-continuous at $x=1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)=2\\ne 4=f(1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement  I is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58795638-a192-5cb2-add6-072256161aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461297} {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bfa1fe-ca62-5b36-b004-861e91cb01da" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7b4c029-937e-5c36-8214-90b1d5fad103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461299} {:answer/id #uuid "a90f0d06-6d6c-5382-abcc-8217128de6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a90f0d06-6d6c-5382-abcc-8217128de6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461300} :answer-field/id #uuid "983a7b3f-b174-5765-9406-806dfae93ca7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58c82481-105a-5321-9ff8-563c4fbcd6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461301} {:answer/id #uuid "a016123d-7112-5014-9f4b-ef79f653d073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58c82481-105a-5321-9ff8-563c4fbcd6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461301} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3cf173a-51b1-50ec-858a-e45fc5b1d0e6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bdde4d8-daa6-55ef-bcc6-21f99b29d77c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104575" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-34, & x<-3 \\\\ -25, & x=-3 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2, & x>-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$\n- **III.** $g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-3$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(-3)=-25$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}({x}^{2}-34)=(-3)^{2}-34=-25, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}({x}^{3}+2)=(-3)^{3}+2=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement I is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25,$ and the value of the function is $g(-3)=-25.$ So, statement II is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the function is continuous at $x=-3,$ and statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed6e077-80c9-5fa7-9d60-8d55f195c7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461303} {:answer/id #uuid "c1761ec4-6ae2-54de-aaef-d153ca2198bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id