wer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86293bdd-1445-5c75-b0fe-3a52f74f9647" :question/math-academy-id "q-104954" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8ff01afa1993f8e301edb69e3e7a13ee71ab01b1a3da416aa53ee94d021184e1.png)\n\nConsider the function $g:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The domain of $g$ is ${0,1,2}$\n- The codomain of $g$ is ${-1,0,1,2}$\n- The range of $g$ is ${0,1,2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X={-1,0,1,2},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y={0,1,2},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is ${0,1,2},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subsets of Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4e84a9-12cc-507d-82ec-e96b850a63c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461389} {:answer/id #uuid "03b2523b-6d7f-5343-be22-5d73eb55caa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e4e84a9-12cc-507d-82ec-e96b850a63c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461389} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f585b3-4b7e-5b0c-950d-f170a9684585" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462448} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e048d875-c5f8-5b05-91e6-d6e57d979a7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461391} {:answer/id #uuid "e7952205-57c2-5868-83de-4486f3e4ba9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7952205-57c2-5868-83de-4486f3e4ba9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461392} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5aee732-4e04-5c86-8c88-17358cec8f30" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af0128c2-64d9-5023-a136-740b0739ee93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461393} {:answer/id #uuid "429ab79c-33d5-501e-9804-0a53e669ec6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af0128c2-64d9-5023-a136-740b0739ee93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461393} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6abdd44-ff6b-5977-869d-6f5e6c1b1f43" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63db395b-88f4-58c0-8886-5830de0a85c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105033" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}_{0}^{-}$ (the set of non-positive rational numbers)?\n\nI. $Z$\n\nII. ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n\nIII. $N$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- $Z$ is *not* a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ For example, $1\\in Z$ but $1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{-}.$\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is  a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ Every negative integer is a non-positive rational number.\n\n- $N$ is *not* a subset of ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$ For example, $1\\in N$ but $1\\notin {Q}_{0}^{-}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b7f1d12-3335-5dd7-bf36-e07077d0c45d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subsets of Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c158a0f0-c079-589b-b013-4a9f9b82fb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461395} {:answer/id #uuid "8744280e-f02c-5bc6-9d15-48facb9c919f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8744280e-f02c-5bc6-9d15-48facb9c919f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461396} :answer-field/id #uuid "2566b0e9-5b7a-5e81-802e-237820ae4fe6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c6a5137-3745-5393-b21d-8c28530d2fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461397} {:answer/id #uuid "65f9100a-2754-5f17-bf7a-2c57cf6cb46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65f9100a-2754-5f17-bf7a-2c57cf6cb46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461398} :answer-field/id #uuid "31f0cff4-3a12-571f-9bd3-e8a1753421a6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc9c1a65-9169-513c-86d2-a12c5bee7636" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461399} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e6960b-0a97-5423-acd7-79f6befe4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8e6960b-0a97-5423-acd7-79f6befe4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461400} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cc0e7a3-af1f-59d7-a52a-6b8ecb9ea699" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb139d93-059f-53af-a8f9-6a747e8ff56b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105034" :question/problem "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n- **I.** ${Q}^{-}$ (the set of negative rationals)\n- **II.** ${Z}^{+}$ (the set of positive integers)\n- **III.** $N$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every negative rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{+}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every positive integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90fd88a2-226a-5ff1-a0a8-df1068304114" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461401} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdbfac7-dcdc-5954-99e7-5bcb06fbfbb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fdbfac7-dcdc-5954-99e7-5bcb06fbfbb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461402} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cddacc-3b19-5547-81a5-439069dd081f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "173f1338-acfe-54fc-b974-a48d7b09e0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461403} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd9d2b5-043e-5936-ab7c-0d5c001ff82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "173f1338-acfe-54fc-b974-a48d7b09e0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461403} :answer-field/id #uuid "17aabf5c-4ef2-5cc0-b531-4d27f7c8830c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe9612a-a9cf-51fb-bb71-2072e7a3766d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461405} {:answer/id #uuid "3e4fbdb2-6ec0-5182-ace8-386026118c59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfe9612a-a9cf-51fb-bb71-2072e7a3766d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461405} :answer-field/id #uuid "06611796-8633-5a59-adc0-f70353fdd9df" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b64d31c-86a0-5b85-a7b4-c7e3f17987a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-105185" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $[4,8]\\cup [10,12]$\n\nII. $[0,5)$\n\nIII. $[1,3)\\cup (3,7]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[4,8]\\cup [10,12]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $4,8,10,$ and $12.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $[0,5)$ has a boundary point $5$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $[1,3)\\cup (3,7]$ has a boundary point $3$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad4656f-44cf-5820-bbb4-4c7080ecfd91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461407} {:answer/id #uuid "8291bfb7-e553-5cc5-921a-0318d746ac71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8291bfb7-e553-5cc5-921a-0318d746ac71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461408} :answer-field/id #uuid "36d255a3-c911-5e54-ace9-938311041b08" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462457} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6f030b6-2173-5ddb-9dce-1e3f1c24d4e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461409} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd96ff2-24b9-5142-9bb1-d5c053f82f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cd96ff2-24b9-5142-9bb1-d5c053f82f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461410} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e2b46a-fe70-5863-8ff5-d490bdab9929" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462458} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b749e21-c8b8-5be6-9cea-8a368496ad79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461411} {:answer/id #uuid "5733ec84-fea9-51fa-a220-df419390ad63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b749e21-c8b8-5be6-9cea-8a368496ad79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461411} :answer-field/id #uuid "105c32c4-df9a-5113-b2f3-701392d57670" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "381adff8-b5e3-59f1-b958-b7182ed98215" :question/math-academy-id "q-105201" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n- **I.** $(2,5)$\n- **II.** $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$\n- **III.** $(-2,2)\\cup (4,10]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(2,5)$ and $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(2,5)$ are $2$, and $5.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(-3,0)\\cup (2,7)$ are $-3$, $0$, $2$, and $7.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(-2,2)\\cup (4,10]$ has four boundary points $-2$, $2$, $4$, and $10$, and the point $10$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b0bd8cc-6ac8-5e72-b06f-73c1654ffe1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461413} {:answer/id #uuid "e80cc002-b38f-5d3e-892e-0841eebc40e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e80cc002-b38f-5d3e-892e-0841eebc40e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461414} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f887e6-6723-5611-bf95-bd986f87144d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81cd52a-c09b-55c3-9802-d94055e5c375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461415} {:answer/id #uuid "4189cfd7-3469-5cbf-a825-c816cd091f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4189cfd7-3469-5cbf-a825-c816cd091f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461416} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa918275-0dac-5d62-b393-8f3adb29993b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462461} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a390f34d-043c-53c1-9c41-c6abbd279b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461417} {:answer/id #uuid "34513fe0-1281-5699-84c3-b63f5d892959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a390f34d-043c-53c1-9c41-c6abbd279b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461417} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f68b655-e005-5eb7-8191-01334bd4f1ec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af32236d-520e-5b71-b7ec-9663a181498c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105310" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n\nII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIII. The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement III is false, while statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124634 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69b456ea-44de-59f0-b2c8-bc5b9495974f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements From a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e569ef55-4f86-5f0f-8e5f-366fbbaf65a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461419} {:answer/id #uuid "9574991b-c705-5663-ad05-8a5ee1ebb134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9574991b-c705-5663-ad05-8a5ee1ebb134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461420} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a9bc66-c7a0-5014-ab05-2056ccacd05b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0905ad9b-9d9b-548c-9b9e-2c65efe682ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461421} {:answer/id #uuid "a348288d-0f17-555e-a70f-b82546994dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0905ad9b-9d9b-548c-9b9e-2c65efe682ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461421} :answer-field/id #uuid "470c3f79-891b-55ed-a428-dd2d5b8e69ec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d009f169-062b-5a05-bfdc-ea900d646a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461423} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d99831-15cf-550e-ab8c-2067bc306a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7d99831-15cf-550e-ab8c-2067bc306a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461424} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4630cd3-7a16-516e-b1f5-3a6fdd6d0b0f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f59eef5f-b761-5dcb-b049-d0c57f2862dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-105313" :question/problem "![](images/da/da3040b284606927a6653bfe18697bff0032dea2647d8d36d857c97472bbc540.png)\n\nConsider the set $M,$ depicted by the shaded region above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n- $B$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n- $C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/c1/c1491f04d1e3d4692dc362008b13ff3909e7ae6f554a5032a9a93036ee2452b5.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $A$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Every open neighborhood of $B$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ The point $B$ is a boundary point for the given set.\n\n- Statement III is true. The point $C$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $C$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and III only'."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078487 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f00fd821-a5d4-5844-9db5-795b9e321b94" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Largest Intervals of Continuity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f5cd349-02df-57a4-87fa-ad7621dc7ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461425} {:answer/id #uuid "c80c29ed-ab88-5f84-a4f6-bfcf8509542b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f5cd349-02df-57a4-87fa-ad7621dc7ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461425} :answer-field/id #uuid "e49eba10-fb5d-5f25-ab9c-eda966fc66dc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80c7e232-9bb0-5a13-b9a9-61d5156eef57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461427} {:answer/id #uuid "e7032692-1def-5667-b369-e6201ffbd33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7032692-1def-5667-b369-e6201ffbd33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461428} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad107a9-8ce8-5886-b6b8-39fdda5e0108" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462467} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace54a21-0486-535d-a83b-20585f9a7047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461429} {:answer/id #uuid "eaef5984-998e-51d8-bebf-b89aaac4b90f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace54a21-0486-535d-a83b-20585f9a7047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461429} :answer-field/id #uuid "78616d03-bd7c-55ad-a15c-d2a4413459e0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bef182d0-f2c3-5147-8c82-4dead855f78c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105418" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b875f560c133e528e4d934ae2722d14c116fac4352f6cca5089f8ec726fe3660.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]$\n- $x\\in [-2,4]$\n- $x\\in [4,\\infty )$\n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,-2].$ Although the function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,-2),$ it is not left-continuous at $x=-2.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $[-2,4].$ It is continuous on $(-2,4),$ and also right-continuous at $x=-2$ and left-continuous at $x=4.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $[4,\\infty ).$ Although the function is continuous on $(4,\\infty ),$ it is not right-continuous at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241051 :knowledge-point/_ques